 * Description:               PROVISIONAL Liberty for AION_mux2i_2
 *
 * Area is the floorplan estimate -- 8 CoreSites x 1.8144 um2 -- and every
 * timing and power table below is sg13g2_mux2_2's, copied verbatim with the
 * unate arcs flipped.  That is deliberate: this file exists so the synthesis
 * mapper has something to read before the cell is drawn.
 *
 * mux2_2 and not mux2_1, because mux2_2 is the PDK cell that makes this
 * cell's trade.  Both take a mux2 core sized for drive 1 and hang a doubled
 * output inverter on it, so both carry the slower internal node that follows;
 * borrowing mux2_1's tables would describe a cell whose output stage is half
 * the size of this one's.
 *
 * It is NOT a characterization, and the borrowed timing fits this cell worse
 * than it would fit a static one.  aion_char's default stimulus is an ideal
 * linear ramp -- a zero-impedance driver -- and this cell has a pass gate on
 * its input path, where the driver stays in series with the transmission gate
 * for the whole transition.  Characterize with --driver-cell before believing
 * any number in here, and never sign anything off against this file.
 * scripts/pdk_cell.py's post-layout stage writes the .lib that replaces it.
 *
 * The cell is INVERTING:  O0 = !(I2 ? I1 : I0), at drive 2.  The PDK has no
 * such cell, so it competes with mux2_1 + inv_2 rather than with mux2_2.
 * cell_footprint is shared with AION_mux2i_1 on purpose -- same function,
 * same pins, different drive, which is what a footprint is for.
 *
 * Pin names follow the cell's own convention:  I0 = A0, I1 = A1, I2 = S.
 * ================================================================ */
